<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ficksburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1867</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ficksburg is a town in the eastern Free State, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caledon-river">Caledon River</a> at the border with Lesotho. It was founded in 1867 on land taken from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sotho-people">Basotho</a> and named after Johan Fick, a Free State commandant in the wars against them. It is known for its cherry orchards.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ficksburg.jpg" alt="Ficksburg" width="320" height="238" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: F. Fouché · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ficksburg_vanaf_Imperani.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
